      "text": {
        "title": "Heute kommt der Arzt",
        "de": "Heute kommt der Arzt auf die Station. Seit Montag liegt der Patient im Zimmer. Am Morgen misst die Pflegekraft das Fieber. Am Morgen liegt der Patient im Zimmer. Heute geht der Patient zum Röntgen. Warum kommt der Arzt? Wo liegt der Patient? Kommt der Arzt heute?",
        "en": "Today the doctor comes onto the ward. The patient has been lying in the room since Monday. In the morning the nurse takes the temperature. In the morning the patient lies in the room. Today the patient goes to X-ray. Why is the doctor coming? Where is the patient lying? Is the doctor coming today?"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "grammar",
      "type": "grammar",
      "label": "Grammar",
      "title": "Position 2",
      "practice": "choose",
      "heroTitle": "The verb keeps its position",
      "heroImage": "ward",
      "story": [
        "Count ideas, not little words. <b>Heute</b> is position 1. <b>kommt</b> is position 2. The subject follows.",
        "A W-question does the same: <b>Wo</b> is position 1, <b>liegt</b> is position 2. A yes/no question has no position 1: the verb itself opens it.",
        "When a sentence has both a time and a place, the neutral order is time first and place late: Am Morgen liegt der Patient <b>im Zimmer</b>."
      ],
      "questionRule": "In these exercises the time word starts the statement. Then the verb, the subject, and the place.",
